// 0115 — forbid with `unless`
//
// New idea: `unless` is sugar for `when !`. Pairing it with a
// `forbid` reads naturally in English: "forbid this action
// unless the request is small."
//
// This rule alone never permits anything (see 0003 for the
// deny-overrides + default-deny rules). Its only job is to
// veto SellShares requests with more than 100 shares. A
// separate `permit` (such as 0001) is still required for the
// request to actually be allowed.

forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"SellShares",
    resource
)
unless { context.input.shares <= 100 };
